@startuml
!include ../../../tools/diagrams/cka-theme.puml
title One NodePort Service: the same port on every node, any Pod behind it

rectangle "client\n<size:11>curl any node IP on :30008</size>" <<plain>> as client

rectangle "node01  192.168.1.2" <<group>> as n1 {
  rectangle ":30008\n<size:11>kube-proxy rules</size>" <<good>> as p1
  rectangle "Pod 10.244.0.2\n<size:11>app=myapp</size>" <<plain>> as a
}
rectangle "node02  192.168.1.3" <<group>> as n2 {
  rectangle ":30008\n<size:11>kube-proxy rules</size>" <<good>> as p2
  rectangle "Pod 10.244.1.3\n<size:11>app=myapp</size>" <<plain>> as b
}
rectangle "node03  192.168.1.4" <<group>> as n3 {
  rectangle ":30008\n<size:11>kube-proxy rules</size>" <<good>> as p3
  rectangle "Pod 10.244.2.4\n<size:11>app=myapp</size>" <<plain>> as c
}

client -down-> p1
client -down-> p2
client -down-> p3
p1 -down-> a
p1 -down-> b
p1 -down-> c
p2 -[hidden]down-> b
p3 -[hidden]down-> c

caption <i>A request reaching node01 can go to a Pod on any node (arrows shown for node01 only; every node has the same rules).</i>\n<i>The Service is one API object with selector app=myapp, whose EndpointSlice lists all three Pods. No Service process runs on the nodes.</i>
@enduml
